		<h2>2. Hosting and server log files</h2>
		<p>This website is hosted on a dedicated server operated by <strong>NexoSystems IT-Solutions (Justin Harth)</strong> in Germany. Hosting is based on our legitimate interest in providing a secure, stable and efficient online service (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>
		<p>When you access the website, the server and the upstream content delivery network automatically collect information transmitted by your browser:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>IP address (shortened or full, depending on the technical configuration)</li>
			<li>date and time of access</li>
			<li>requested URL and referrer URL</li>
			<li>browser type, browser version and operating system</li>
			<li>amount of data transferred and HTTP status code</li>
			<li>error messages and security events, where applicable</li>
		</ul>
		<p>This processing is used for technical delivery, system security, error analysis and defence against attacks. Server log files are generally deleted after no more than <strong>14 days</strong>, unless they are needed for longer to investigate a specific security incident or to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</p>

		<h2>3. Cloudflare</h2>
		<p>The domain novroforge.xyz is served through the content delivery network and security services of <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> (101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). Cloudflare processes technical connection data, in particular IP address, request and response data, browser information and security and performance metrics, in order to deliver the website and protect it against attacks. For more information, please see Cloudflare's privacy policy.</p>
		<p>This processing is based on our legitimate interest in a secure and high-performance service (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare may transfer data to the United States. Such transfers are based on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses and, where applicable, the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>

		<h2>4. Registration, user account and login</h2>
		<p>You may create a user account to use the platform. We process in particular:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>username and display name</li>
			<li>email address</li>
			<li>password (stored only as a salted hash, never in plain text)</li>
			<li>profile information you provide voluntarily (e.g. name, website, location, pronouns, biography, avatar)</li>
			<li>authentication and session data as well as security-related logs</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Processing is necessary to perform the user agreement (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and also serves the security of your account and the platform (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Without this information, we cannot provide a user account.</p>

		<h2>5. Repositories, issues, comments and other content</h2>
		<p>If you create repositories, issues, pull requests, comments, wiki pages, releases or other content, we process that content to provide the service. Public repositories and public profile information are visible to all visitors. Private repositories are accessible only to you and the persons you authorise. Git commit metadata (e.g. name and email address in a commit) may be publicly visible when you push commits to public repositories.</p>
		<p>The legal basis is the performance of the user agreement (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and our legitimate interest in providing and securing the platform (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>

		<h2>6. Cookies and local storage</h2>
		<p>We use technically necessary cookies and local storage to provide login, sessions, language settings and security functions. These include session and CSRF protection cookies in particular. They are necessary for the operation of the website and are processed on the basis of Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR and Section 25(2) TDDDG.</p>
		<p>Cloudflare may set its own technically necessary cookies for attack detection and security. We currently do not use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

		<h2>7. Communication</h2>
		<p>If you contact us by email, we process your information to handle the request and for any follow-up questions. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the request relates to the performance of a contract and otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The data is deleted once the request has been finally processed and no statutory retention obligations apply.</p>

		<h2>8. Legal bases at a glance</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR:</strong> performance of a contract and pre-contractual measures (account, repositories, support).</li>
			<li><strong>Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR:</strong> legitimate interests (operation, security, abuse prevention, technical error analysis).</li>
			<li><strong>Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR:</strong> legal obligations (e.g. retention, legal enforcement).</li>
			<li><strong>Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR:</strong> consent, where we obtain it.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>9. Recipients and transfers to third countries</h2>
		<p>Recipients of data include the hosting provider, Cloudflare's CDN and, where applicable, technical service providers commissioned by us. Data is disclosed only where permitted by law or with your consent. Transfers to third countries take place only on the basis of appropriate safeguards (in particular Standard Contractual Clauses) or a statutory exception. Cloudflare may transfer data to the United States; such transfers are covered by the safeguards mentioned above.</p>

