		<h2>10. Retention period</h2>
		<p>We store personal data only for as long as necessary for the respective purposes or as required by statutory retention obligations. Account and content data remains stored until the account or content is deleted. Server log files are regularly deleted after no more than 14 days. Statutory retention periods (in particular under commercial and tax law) remain unaffected.</p>

		<h2>11. Your rights</h2>
		<p>Subject to the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
			<li>rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
			<li>erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
			<li>restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
			<li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
			<li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
			<li>withdraw consent (Art. 7(3) GDPR)</li>
		</ul>
		<p>To exercise your rights, simply contact us at the email address above.</p>

		<h2>12. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
		<p>You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in particular the authority at your place of residence or habitual residence and the authority responsible for the controller. An overview of the supervisory authorities in Germany is available from the German Data Protection Conference (Datenschutzkonferenz).</p>

		<h2>13. Data security</h2>
		<p>We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against loss, destruction, unauthorised access and unauthorised alteration. These include encrypted connections (TLS), hashed passwords, access restrictions and regular security updates. However, absolute security in data transmission over the internet cannot be guaranteed.</p>

		<h2>14. Security incidents and data misuse</h2>
		<p>We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data. If a security incident, data loss, unauthorised access or data misuse nevertheless occurs, we will investigate it without undue delay, take containment measures and comply with our notification obligations under Art. 33 and 34 GDPR. Where there is a high risk to the rights and freedoms of affected individuals, we will inform them without undue delay. Suspicious activity, security vulnerabilities or data misuse can be reported to the contact address above at any time. In the case of criminal offences, we reserve the right to involve the competent authorities.</p>

		<h2>15. No automated decision-making</h2>
		<p>No automated decision-making, including profiling within the meaning of Art. 22 GDPR, takes place.</p>

		<h2>16. Minors</h2>
